otp_socket (lwIP): callbacks without a socket; partial and full sends

Found bringing AtomVM up on the Elixos coprocessor firmware (bare metal,
lwIP 2.2.1 NO_SYS, epmd and distribution over loopback and a point-to-point
netif):

- After socket:close/1 the pcb lives on (FIN, TIME_WAIT) with tcp_arg NULL
  but tcp_err_cb still registered; a reset then calls it with arg NULL and
  it dereferences it (load fault at address -8). Close now unregisters the
  err callback (listening pcbs have none) and the recv callback (lwIP's
  default frees late data), and tcp_err_cb ignores a pcb without a socket.
- An accepted pcb has tcp_arg NULL until its owner calls accept. Data the
  client sends at once (epmd's ALIVE2_REQ right after connect) was queued,
  found no resource and was dropped, so registration never got an answer.
  tcp_recv_cb now refuses it (ERR_MEM): lwIP keeps it as refused_data and
  offers it again on its next timer tick, by when accept has run.
- tcp_recv_handler frees the pbuf of a socket closed meanwhile.
- do_socket_send queued at most one MSS per call, so socket:send/2 of
  anything larger returned {ok, Rest}; with the send buffer full it
  returned SocketWouldBlock, which nif_socket_send_internal turned into
  {error, closed}. It now queues as much as tcp_sndbuf allows, an MSS at a
  time, and a full buffer answers {ok, Data} (a 10 kB distribution reply
  never arrived before).
- A platform may define OTP_SOCKET_LWIP_NODELAY to create every TCP pcb
  with Nagle off. There is no {tcp, nodelay} option on lwIP; distribution
  (which OTP runs with nodelay) otherwise waits out the peer's delayed ACK:
  erpc round trips took 44 ms over a link that pings in 1.2 ms.

